title: Getting started with the Hive plugin

This is a minimal wiki for testing the Hive storage plugin.

! Testing the plugin

# Install the [[https://github.com/hivewallet/hive-keychain|Hive Keychain]] browser extension.
# Open the ''Control Panel'' and go to the ''Hive'' tab.
# Enter your Hive account name and press ''Save to Hive''.
# The Keychain extension asks you to sign the transaction. Nothing is sent to the blockchain before you sign it.
# Open the URL that is shown in the ''Post'' field to see the result on Hive.

! The tiddlers of this wiki

The tiddlers of this wiki are published as one reply each, all as direct replies of the root post of the wiki. The parent/child relations between the tiddlers are stored in the metadata of each reply, not in the structure of the replies on Hive.

! Loading a single post as a tiddler

The ''hivelink'' procedure renders a link that loads a Hive post into this wiki as a tiddler:

```
<<hivelink accountId permlink "Caption">>
```

* ''accountId'': the Hive account the post belongs to (a leading ''@'' is allowed)
* ''permlink'': the permlink of the post
* ''Caption'' (optional): the label of the link, defaults to the permlink

Clicking the link loads the post from the Hive blockchain and opens it in the story. Everything that was loaded this way carries the tag ''$:/hive/external'':

* ''Save to Hive'' ignores tagged tiddlers, so reading posts never gets anything published by accident.
* The tiddlers are still kept in this wiki, they survive a refresh.
* The type of the tiddler follows the type that is declared in the ''json_metadata'' of the post: markdown is the default, and posts that declare html (mixed html/markdown included) are served as ''text/html''.
* When the post was loaded before, the link checks the ''last_update'' timestamp of the post and only reloads the tiddler when the post actually changed.

When the wiki is saved to Hive, the ''hivelink'' calls are published as ordinary links to the Hive front-end: `<<hivelink accountId permlink "Caption">>` becomes the markdown link `[Caption](https://hive.blog/accountId/permlink)` in the body of the post.

! Notes

* Publishing is always explicit: nothing is sent to the blockchain until you press the ''Save to Hive'' button.
* The canonical text of a tiddler is stored in the metadata of its reply, so the wiki is restored exactly as it was.
* Use the ''Load from Hive'' button to read the wiki back into this wiki. Set the ''Pull mode'' to ''Only add missing tiddlers'' if you want to keep the tiddlers that are already here.
